// BT-3535 (ADR 0123 Phase 1 spike): proves the one mechanism ADR 0123's
// general migration chain (Phase 2) rests on — that
// beamtalk_object_class:local_call/3 can be invoked from inside
// beamtalk_hot_reload:code_change/3 while the reloading class's own
// module is mid-reload — during a real `:load` reload of a live instance,
// not a synthetic/standalone call.
//
// v1 has no migration hook. v2 adds `total` and a class-side
// `migrateFromV1:` that computes it from `itemCount` (* 10) — a value the
// structural fallback's plain default (0) could never produce. A live
// instance surviving the reload with the *hook-computed* total (not 0) is
// direct proof the hook ran, via local_call/3, against v2's own
// just-swapped module code — code:load_binary/3 has already run by the
// time code_change/3 (and this probe inside it) fires, so local_call/3
// resolves the *new* module, not the old one.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Load v1 (no hook) and spawn a live instance
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

:load tests/repl-protocol/fixtures/hot_shape_hook_cart.bt
// => Loaded: HotShapeHookCart

cart := HotShapeHookCart spawn
// => Actor(HotShapeHookCart, _)

cart addItem
// => 1

cart addItem
// => 2

cart addItem
// => 3

cart getItemCount
// => 3

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Reload with v2: adds `total` + `class migrateFromV1:`. The live instance
// above predates `total` entirely, so the migration hook — not the
// structural fallback's default — must supply its value.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

:load tests/repl-protocol/fixtures/hot_shape_hook_cart_v2.bt
// => Loaded: HotShapeHookCart

// itemCount survives the reload unchanged.
cart getItemCount
// => 3

// total is hook-computed (itemCount * 10 = 30), not the structural
// fallback's plain default of 0 — proof that migrateFromV1: actually ran,
// via local_call/3, against the reloading class's new module.
cart getTotal
// => 30
